# UserActivityAudit — Commercial Production Mode

## Product scope
- Commercial-grade user activity audit for Windows 10/11 (pilot fleet: 15 laptops).
- **Not** a prototype. No "we'll fix later" stubs in merged code.
- Full stack: C++ agent (L1+L2+L3), minifilter driver, server (ingest/escrow/alerts/portal), C# admin suite.

## Architecture rules
- **Client (native/)**: C++20 only. Windows Service. Target ≤15 MB RAM on 2 GB PCs (Low profile).
- **Server (server/)**: C# .NET 10 — ingest, escrow, alerts, web portal.
- **Admin (admin/)**: C# .NET 10 — WPF dashboard, reports, forensic, LogImporter.
- **No .NET on client laptops.**

## Development workflow
- Work **one ROADMAP phase at a time**. Do not skip ahead.
- Each module: production error handling, config-driven, unit tests where applicable.
- Code comments: English. User-facing docs and git commit messages: Russian.
- Update ROADMAP.md when a phase/sprint is completed.
- Minimize diff scope; match existing conventions.

## Security (non-negotiable)
- Logs: AES-256-GCM at rest, DEK split (TPM + USB), server escrow, HMAC hash chain.
- Tamper: minifilter + IT USB Ed25519 for uninstall/stop (Phase 5+).
- No hardcoded secrets. No plaintext logs on disk after Phase 2.
- Keylog/screenshots: opt-in modules only; off by default.

## Out of scope unless explicitly requested
- Prototype shortcuts (plaintext logs, hardcoded config, skip tests).
- Simplifying to "network share only" instead of server stack.
- Committing unless user asks.

